        "column_yta9hD": {
          "type": "column",
          "settings": {
            "title": "&nbsp;Replace Your Car&nbsp;",
            "text": "<p>Most everyday Canadian trips are short. A Kodiak covers grocery runs, school pickups, and neighbourhood errands without parking fees or gas. Top speed <strong>32 km/h</strong>. In BC, the Kodiak lineup is eligible for the <strong>SUVI</strong> rebate — up to <strong>$858 CAD</strong> if you qualify.<br/><br/></p>",
            "link_label": "",
            "link": ""
          }
        },
        "column_iLKUfU": {
          "type": "column",
          "settings": {
            "title": "&nbsp;Built to Carry&nbsp;",
            "text": "<p>Both racks are rated up to <strong>120 lb</strong>. Kodiak includes a large bamboo platform and a UL 2271–certified 19.6Ah Samsung pack. Kodiak V2 adds an extra-long rack, integrated 20Ah battery, and optional front basket / rear passenger bars.<br/><br/></p>",
            "link_label": "",
            "link": ""
          }
        },
        "column_qf6bGz": {
          "type": "column",
          "settings": {
            "title": "&nbsp;Versatile Platforms&nbsp;",
            "text": "<p>One bike for groceries, commuting with gear, trails-to-town rides, a second passenger with the right accessories, or local last-mile deliveries. Compact enough for apartments, garages, and underground parking.<br/><br/></p>",
            "link_label": "",
            "link": ""
          }
        }
      },
